{"id":"ccaaf599ec318a33","group":"58","path":"58/batch05/58-df-knot.md","title":"Knot","display":"df-knot — Knot","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-knot","aliases":["58-df-knot","Knot"],"display":"df-knot — Knot","depends_on":["[[../batch08/58-df-sphere.md]]","[[../batch13/58-df-zfc-top2-topological-embedding.md]]","[[../batch03/58-df-euclidean-topological-data.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-knot"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-knot</span><span>Knot</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-knot — Knot"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ed44d43cf74ca35e\" href=\"?note=ed44d43cf74ca35e\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-sphere.md\">../batch08/58-df-sphere.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"890a8458fc69d8c7\" href=\"?note=890a8458fc69d8c7\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-zfc-top2-topological-embedding.md\">../batch13/58-df-zfc-top2-topological-embedding.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"ca7fc3ab38a11801\" href=\"?note=ca7fc3ab38a11801\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-euclidean-topological-data.md\">../batch03/58-df-euclidean-topological-data.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\\in V\">\\(k\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S^{(-)}:\\omega\\to V\">\\(S^{(-)}:\\omega\\to V\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"ed44d43cf74ca35e\" href=\"?note=ed44d43cf74ca35e\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-sphere.md\">../batch08/58-df-sphere.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_{\\mathbb R^{(-)}}=\\{\\langle n,\\mathrm{EuclideanSubspaceTopology}_S(\\mathbb R^n,n)\\rangle:n\\in\\omega\\}\">\\(\\tau_{\\mathbb R^{(-)}}=\\{\\langle n,\\mathrm{EuclideanSubspaceTopology}_S(\\mathbb R^n,n)\\rangle:n\\in\\omega\\}\\)</span>。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcTop2TopologicalEmbedding}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcTop2TopologicalEmbedding}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"890a8458fc69d8c7\" href=\"?note=890a8458fc69d8c7\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-zfc-top2-topological-embedding.md\">../batch13/58-df-zfc-top2-topological-embedding.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Knot}_S:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\operatorname{Knot}_S:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}knot}\\vdash \\operatorname{Knot}_S(k)\\leftrightarrow\\exists\\tau_1,\\tau_3\\;\\left(\\tau_1=\\{U\\cap S^1:U\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb R^2}\\}\\land\\tau_3=\\{U\\cap S^3:U\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb R^4}\\}\\land\\mathrm{ZfcTop2TopologicalEmbedding}_S(k,S^1,\\tau_1,S^3,\\tau_3)\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}knot}\\vdash \\operatorname{Knot}_S(k)\\leftrightarrow\\exists\\tau_1,\\tau_3\\;\\left(\\tau_1=\\{U\\cap S^1:U\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb R^2}\\}\\land\\tau_3=\\{U\\cap S^3:U\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb R^4}\\}\\land\\mathrm{ZfcTop2TopologicalEmbedding}_S(k,S^1,\\tau_1,S^3,\\tau_3)\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>A knot is an embedding <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S^1\\hookrightarrow S^3\">\\(S^1\\hookrightarrow S^3\\)</span>; an ambient-isotopy class is a knot type.</li>\n<li>Ambient isotopy equivalence of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\">\\(k\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k&#39;\">\\(k&#39;\\)</span> may be expressed by an isotopy <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"h:S^3\\times I\\to S^3\">\\(h:S^3\\times I\\to S^3\\)</span> with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"h_0=\\mathrm{id}\">\\(h_0=\\mathrm{id}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"h_1(k[S^1])=k&#39;[S^1]\">\\(h_1(k[S^1])=k&#39;[S^1]\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The knot group is the derived invariant <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi_1(S^3\\setminus k[S^1])\">\\(\\pi_1(S^3\\setminus k[S^1])\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The exterior <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S^3\\setminus N(k[S^1])\">\\(S^3\\setminus N(k[S^1])\\)</span> has torus boundary.</li>\n<li>Prime: indecomposable under connected sum; JSJ decomposition via torus</li>\n<li>Satellite: composite of prime knots via companion; splice; determines hierarchy</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Adams, The Knot Book</li>\n<li>Rolfsen, Knots and Links</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch08/58-df-sphere.md","status":"resolved","id":"ed44d43cf74ca35e","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-df-sphere.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-zfc-top2-topological-embedding.md","status":"resolved","id":"890a8458fc69d8c7","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-zfc-top2-topological-embedding.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch03/58-df-euclidean-topological-data.md","status":"resolved","id":"ca7fc3ab38a11801","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch03/58-df-euclidean-topological-data.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch08/58-df-sphere.md","status":"resolved","id":"ed44d43cf74ca35e","a